@startuml
autoactivate on
autonumber

actor "User" as User
participant ":System" as System
participant "Spotify" as Spotify
participant "Deezer" as Deezer
participant "iTunes" as iTunes

activate User

User -> System: asks to play the preview of a track
alt preview already known for this track
  System --> User: plays the preview
else not known yet
  System -> Spotify: asks for the ISRC of the track
  Spotify --> System: returns the ISRC (or none)
  System -> Deezer: looks the preview up by ISRC
  Deezer --> System: returns the preview URL (or none)
  opt none found
    System -> Deezer: searches by artist and track title
    Deezer --> System: returns the candidates
  end
  opt none found
    System -> iTunes: searches by artist and track title
    iTunes --> System: returns the candidates
  end
  alt preview of the same recording available
    System --> User: plays the preview and shows the pause button
  else not available
    System --> User: informs that the preview is unavailable
  else every source failed
    System --> User: informs that the preview failed
  end
end

User -> System: asks to pause the preview
System --> User: pauses the preview
User -> System: asks to resume the preview
System --> User: resumes the preview
User -> System: taps the button while the preview is loading
System --> User: cancels the loading

note right of System
  Only one track plays at a time (30 s).
  A candidate is accepted only if title, artist and
  duration (within 5 s) match the Spotify track.
  The preview stops when it ends or when
  the app goes to the background.
end note
@enduml
